Now I'm acting as Crew. Let me follow the skill:

1. Verify dispatch matches contract - I have the target (features/todomvc-conformance.feature:Toggling a todo mutates existing DOM nodes in place) and failure evidence (todoList.innerHTML = html; at line 101).

2. First pass: Read RIGGING.md (done), the feature file (done).

3. Second pass: Read step definitions (done), production files (done, js/app.js).

4. State the target and durable source of expected behaviour.

The target: Toggling a todo must mutate existing DOM nodes in place. No `todoList.innerHTML =` assignment.

The fix: Instead of replacing `todoList.innerHTML`, I need to mutate the DOM in-place - remove/add children, update classes, etc., or use DOM manipulation methods.

Let me look at the render function in js/app.js more carefully. The current approach:

```javascript
var html = '';
for (var i = 0; i < filtered.length; i++) {
  var todo = filtered[i];
  var liClass = '';
  if (todo.completed) liClass += ' completed';
  var checkedAttr = todo.completed ? 'checked' : '';
  html += '<li data-id="' + todo.id + '" class="' + liClass + '">';
  html += '<div class="view">';
  html += '<input class="toggle" type="checkbox" ' + checkedAttr + '>';
  html += '<label>' + escapeHtml(todo.title) + '</label>';
  html += '<button class="destroy"></button>';
  html += '</div>';
  html += '<input class="edit" value="' + escapeHtml(todo.title) + '">';
  html += '</li>';
}
todoList.innerHTML = html;
```

I need to replace this with DOM manipulation that reuses existing nodes where possible, or at minimum creates nodes via document methods rather than innerHTML.

